        "original_id": "99e5f9ca-bd1d-5d7d-9f7c-d6b2fe187b95",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Belgium, Lausanne, Switzerland, Lake Geneva\n- People: Ingeborg\n- Events: Eurovision Song Contest 1989\n- Products: \"Door de wind\"\n\nFacts:\n- On 6 May 1989, the 1989 Eurovision Song Contest took place in Lausanne, Switzerland.\n- At the 1989 Eurovision Song Contest, Belgium was represented by Ingeborg with the song \"Door de wind\".\n- Lausanne is situated on the shores of Lake Geneva.\n- Lake Geneva is called \"Lac Léman\" in French and is also simply called \"Le Léman\".",
